      "error_message": "POST /api/auth/registration-options 400 (Bad Request) at WebAuthn.kt:105",
      "file": "frontend/src/jsMain/kotlin/com/adoptu/frontend/pages/RegisterPage.kt",
      "root_cause": "Re-submitting the registration form with an email already in the system (e.g. testing multiple role/profile combos with the same test address) correctly returns HTTP 400 from AuthRoutes.kt with an informational message (\"email already registered\" or \"verification email sent. Check your inbox.\"). This is expected backend behavior, not a defect - but registerPasskey/registerPassword/registerBoth in RegisterPage.kt unconditionally prefixed every caught error with \"Error: \", so the informational message rendered as \"Error: verification email sent...\", making a normal duplicate-registration case look like a broken endpoint.",
