      "root_cause": "UserRepository.getById()/getByEmail()/getAllUsers() built UserDto without mapping user[Users.isEmailVerified], so isEmailVerified silently defaulted to false for every caller of getById/getByEmail/getAllUsers (the /api/auth/me endpoint was unaffected since it calls webAuthnService.isUserVerified() -> a separate direct-query repository method). Separately, the activation-gate check was written before the existing-user lookup, so a nonexistent session user hit the verification 403 instead of falling through to the existing 404.",
